<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis weakens at U.S. Gulf.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis weakens at U.S. Gulf.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat continued to weaken on Wednesday with levels at the U.S. Gulf leading the way, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>The basis at Galveston, Texas, was down five cents at 35 cents over May KCBT futures, with export demand remaining slow.</p>
<p>Dealers noted the recent rise in flat prices had sparked enough farmer selling to satisfy current weak demand. There also continued to be switching from May to July KCBT futures as the basis for nearby bids.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a little bit of movement, just enough to take care of what demand there is,&quot; one Kansas dealer said.</p>
